[{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Describe the following linear transformations:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\3&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-4\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\-\\frac32&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>A shape with area 4 is mapped to its image by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;6\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Write down the area of the shape’s image.</p>","steps":["<p>This is a shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so area is preserved. Hence the area of the shape’s image is 4 units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, which maps <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(18,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;k\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}18\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}-2+4k\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}18\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2+4k=18\\Rightarrow k=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, which maps <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(22,-6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(22,-94)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}22\\\\-6\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}22\\\\-94\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}22\\\\22k-6\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}22\\\\-94\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22k-6=-94\\Rightarrow k=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has vertices at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,\\sqrt2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3\\sqrt2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\sqrt2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is transformed by a shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8\\sqrt2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using matrices, find the exact coordinates of the vertices of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and hence show that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the same as the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has area</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times7\\sqrt2\\times\\sqrt2=7\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;8\\sqrt2\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;-3\\sqrt2&amp;4\\sqrt2\\\\\\sqrt2&amp;0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}15&amp;-3\\sqrt2&amp;4\\sqrt2\\\\\\sqrt2&amp;0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has vertices at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(15,\\sqrt2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3\\sqrt2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\sqrt2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  Triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has area</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times7\\sqrt2\\times\\sqrt2=7\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,3\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,5\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\3\\sqrt3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\5\\sqrt3\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\8k+3\\sqrt3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\5\\sqrt3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8k+3\\sqrt3=5\\sqrt3\\Rightarrow8k=2\\sqrt3\\Rightarrow k=\\frac{\\sqrt3}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}4&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(50,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;k\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}50\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}50+4k\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50+4k=4\\Rightarrow4k=-46\\Rightarrow k=-\\frac{23}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-\\frac{23}2\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(45,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to a point that lies on the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;k\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}45\\\\9\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\p\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}45+9k\\\\9\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\p\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45+9k=0\\Rightarrow9k=-45\\Rightarrow k=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-5\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, which maps the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to itself, and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,20)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(11,20)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to itself, the shear must fix the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;k\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}11\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}3+20k\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}11\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3+20k=11\\Rightarrow20k=8\\Rightarrow k=\\frac25\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;\\frac25\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, which maps the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,17)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents a shear, which maps the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,17)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\\mathbf B=\\mathbf I\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,17)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the shear must fix the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\17\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\-12k+8\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\17\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-12k+8=17\\Rightarrow-12k=9\\Rightarrow k=-\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\-\\frac34&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,17)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-12,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the shear must fix the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\17\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\-12k+17\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-12\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-12k+17=8\\Rightarrow-12k=-9\\Rightarrow k=\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf B=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\\\frac34&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\\mathbf B=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\-\\frac34&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\\\frac34&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\times1+0\\times\\frac34&amp;1\\times0+0\\times1\\\\-\\frac34\\times1+1\\times\\frac34&amp;-\\frac34\\times0+1\\times1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}=\\mathbf I\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The vertices of a parallelogram <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(4,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(7,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(5,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The parallelogram is mapped to quadrilateral <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'B'C'D'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, as shown in the diagram below, by the shear associated with matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,8.25)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/139-q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>The transformation is a shear, and clearly it is with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;4&amp;7&amp;5\\\\2&amp;6&amp;6&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;c&amp;5\\\\d&amp;e&amp;f&amp;8.25\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;4&amp;7&amp;5\\\\2k+2&amp;4k+6&amp;7k+6&amp;5k+2\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;c&amp;5\\\\d&amp;e&amp;f&amp;8.25\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=2, b=4, c=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5k+2=8.25\\Rightarrow k=1.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\1.25&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'(2,4.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B'(4,11)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C'(7,14.75)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>The vertices of a trapezium <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(-5,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-5,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(-1,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The parallelogram is mapped to the trapezium <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'B'C'D'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, as shown in the diagram below, by the shear associated with the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B'\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C'\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/139-q12.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>The transformation is a shear, and clearly it is with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;k\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;-5&amp;-5&amp;-1\\\\3&amp;6&amp;9&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;c&amp;5\\\\d&amp;e&amp;f&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\begin{pmatrix}-1+3k&amp;-5+6k&amp;-5+9k&amp;-1+9k\\\\3&amp;6&amp;9&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;c&amp;5\\\\d&amp;e&amp;f&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore d=3, e=6, f=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1+9k=5\\Rightarrow k=\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;\\frac23\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A'(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B'(-1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C'(1,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.39-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\k&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>describe the linear transformation associated with the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By considering <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, describe two properties of the transformation associated with the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Shear, with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis fixed, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mapped to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=1\\times1-0\\times k=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det\\mathbf A=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, both area and orientation are preserved by the transformation.</p>"]}]